 "brief_summary": "The purpose of this study is to explore whether the novel therapy of type 2 diabetes, vildagliptin, which inhibits dipeptidyl peptidase-4 (DPP-4), affects glucagon counterregulation during hypoglycemia in insulin-treated patients with type 2 diabetes. Vildagliptin is given, together with the on-going insulin therapy, for one month, whereafter hypoglycemia is induced under standardized conditions, and the glucagon response is determined, and compared to that after a month of placebo treatment.",
